stateDiagram-v2
  accTitle: Controller state transitions with the accumulate path and cycle accounting
  accDescr: Synchronous active-low reset takes any state to IDLE. Start is accepted only in IDLE or DONE, with k_len and accumulate sampled at the same edge. A normal start goes to CLEAR; an accumulate start goes straight to COMPUTE, keeping the previous accumulators. CLEAR and CAPTURE each last one cycle. COMPUTE runs steps zero through T minus one, with T equal to k_len plus 2N minus 2. DONE persists until another start.

  state "IDLE<br/>busy = 0; done = 0<br/>hold while !start" as IDLE
  state "CLEAR<br/>busy = 1; clear = 1<br/>1 cycle" as CLEAR
  state "COMPUTE<br/>busy = 1; en = 1<br/>step = 0 … T − 1" as COMPUTE
  state "CAPTURE<br/>busy = 1; capture = 1<br/>1 cycle" as CAPTURE
  state "DONE<br/>busy = 0; done = 1<br/>hold while !start<br/>cycle_count = T + 2 (T + 1 if accumulate)" as DONE

  [*] --> IDLE: synchronous reset
  IDLE --> IDLE
  IDLE --> CLEAR: start & !accumulate
  IDLE --> COMPUTE: start & accumulate
  CLEAR --> COMPUTE
  COMPUTE --> COMPUTE: step != T − 1
  COMPUTE --> CAPTURE: step == T − 1
  CAPTURE --> DONE
  DONE --> DONE
  DONE --> CLEAR: start & !accumulate
  DONE --> COMPUTE: start & accumulate

  note left of IDLE
    Any state + !rst_n at rising clk:
    IDLE; step = 0; cycle_count = 0
    Unlisted control outputs = 0
    start with k_len = 0 or k_len > K_MAX
    is ignored; busy stays low
  end note
  note left of COMPUTE
    T = k_len + 2N − 2 (22 for k_len = K_MAX = 16, N = 4)
    k_len, accumulate sampled with start;
    run_k_len held for the run
    start ignored while busy
    step increments on self-loop; 0 elsewhere
    Accepted start zeroes cycle_count
    Each busy edge increments cycle_count
    cycle_count holds T + 2 in DONE,
    or T + 1 after an accumulate run
  end note
